== Rolling stock ==
Okami Metro operates a diverse fleet of rolling stock tailored to the specific technical requirements of its lines. The majority of the network utilizes standard third-rail electrification (750 V DC). However, the [[Kita Line]], [[Nagata Line]], and [[Imaichi Line]] utilize overhead catenary systems (1,500 V DC) to facilitate through-service with suburban commuter rail lines and to accommodate linear motor propulsion.

The newest addition to the fleet is the 4000 Series, introduced in 2023 on the [[Miyoshi Line]] and [[Chūō Line (Okami)|Chūō Line]]. These trains feature a futuristic design reminiscent of a spacecraft, with hexagonal windows and onboard Wi-Fi integrated with the city's Satori Network. They were specifically commissioned to serve as the face of the transport network for the upcoming Expo.

